efining boundaries, ownership, trust, storage, threat model, and gap analysis, and a second implementable design round defining DTOs, entities, options, interfaces, endpoint contracts, reason codes, audit payloads, XMLDoc obligations, and test mappings.\\u0022,\\u0022WorkspaceId\\u0022:\\u0022F:\\\\\\\\GitHub\\\\\\\\McpServer\\u0022,\\u0022Priority\\u0022:\\u0022medium\\u0022,\\u0022Status\\u0022:\\u0022pending\\u0022,\\u0022Notes\\u0022:null,\\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\\u0022:[{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022\\u0022,\\u0022text\\u0022:\\u0022\\\\u0060TurnTransactions-Architecture-Round1.md\\\\u0060 captures component boundaries, trust model, storage boundaries, rollback/audit rules, threat model, and gap analysis.\\u0022,\\u0022isSatisfied\\u0022:true,\\u0022evidence\\u0022:null},{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022\\u0022,\\u0022text\\u0022:\\u0022\\\\u0060TurnTransactions-Design-Round2.md\\\\u0060 captures implementable DTOs, entities, options, interfaces, endpoint contracts, reason codes, canonicalization, audit payloads, XMLDoc obligations, and TEST-MCP-158 through TEST-MCP-173 mappings.\\u0022,\\u0022isSatisfied\\u0022:true,\\u0022evidence\\u0022:null},{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022\\u0022,\\u0022text\\u0022:\\u0022\\\\u0060TurnTransactions-Mutation-Endpoint-Audit.md\\\\u0060 captures current gated, fail-closed, and explicitly deferred mutation surfaces.\\u0022,\\u0022isSatisfied\\u0022:true,\\u0022evidence\\u0022:null},{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022\\u0022,\\u0022text\\u0022:\\u0022Requirements matrix and FR/TR mapping rows link FR-MCP-118 through FR-MCP-128 to transaction TR and TEST records.\\u0022,\\u0022isSatisfied\\u0022:true,\\u0022evidence\\u0022:null}],\\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\\u0022:\\u0022layer-1\\u0022,\\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\\u0022:null,\\u0022LinkedUseCases\\u0022:[]},{\\u0022Id\\u0022:\\u0022FR-MCP-129\\u0022,\\u0022Title\\u0022:\\u0022Durable external brain-slot registry and live invocation\\u0022,\\u0022Body\\u0022:\\u0022The MCP runtime SHALL provide durable workspace-scoped external brain-slot definitions for LeftHemisphere, RightHemisphere, CuriosityEngine, and ArbiterOfTruth, including CRUD, readiness status projection, and individually gated live model invocation.\\u0022,\\u0022WorkspaceId\\u0022:\\u0022F:\\\\\\\\GitHub\\\\\\\\McpServer\\u0022,\\u0022Priority\\u0022:\\u0022critical\\u0022,\\u0022Status\\u0022:\\u0022completed\\u0022,\\u0022Notes\\u0022:\\u0022External brain slot runtime plus full Quad-Brain orchestration authorization is complete; implicit fallback remains fail-closed.\\u0022,\\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\\u0022:[{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022AC-FR-MCP-129-001\\u0022,\\u0022text\\u0022:\\u0022Brain-slot definitions are durable CRUD records scoped by workspace and role.\\u0022,\\u0022isSatisfied\\u0022:true,\\u0022evidence\\u0022:null},{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022AC-FR-MCP-129-002\\u0022,\\u0022text\\u0022:\\u0022Exactly one enabled slot per workspace and role is allowed; enabling a replacement requires replaceExisting=true and writes an audit entry.\\u0022,\\u0022isSatisfied\\u0022:true,\\u0022evidence\\u0022:null},{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022AC-FR-MCP-129-003\\u0022,\\u0022text\\u0022:\\u0022A workspace is quad-ready only when all four roles have enabled slots with valid provider, model, endpoint policy, credential reference, and trusted party mapping.\\u0022,\\u0022isSatisfied\\u0022:true,\\u0022evidence\\u0022:null},{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022AC-FR-MCP-129-004\\u0022,\\u0022text\\u0022:\\u0022CRUD stores and returns credentialReference only; raw API keys are never persisted or returned.\\u0022,\\u0022isSatisfied\\u0022:true,\\u0022evidence\\u0022:null},{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022AC-FR-MCP-129-005\\u0022,\\u0022text\\u0022:\\u0022REST, client, and STDIO/MCP surfaces expose list/get/upsert/delete/enable/disable/status/invoke parity.\\u0022,\\u0022isSatisfied\\u0022:true,\\u0022evidence\\u0022:null},{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022AC-FR-MCP-129-006\\u0022,\\u0022text\\u0022:\\u0022Invocation is rejected unless brain-slot execution is enabled, the slot is enabled, endpoint policy passes, credentials resolve, and required turn transactions are enabled.\\u0022,\\u0022isSatisfied\\u0022:true,\\u0022evidence\\u0022:null},{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022AC-FR-MCP-129-007\\u0022,\\u0022text\\u0022:\\u0022No implicit fallback model is used; fallback behavior remains fail-closed with structured reason codes unless a configured slot is invoked and committed.\\u0022,\\u0022isSatisfied\\u0022:true,\\u0022evidence\\u0022:null}],\\u0022ScopeStartLayerKey\\u0022:\\u0022layer-1\\u0022,\\u0022ScopeEndLayerKey\\u0022:null,\\u0022LinkedUseCases\\u0022:[]},{\\u0022Id\\u0022:\\u0022FR-MCP-130\\u0022,\\u0022Title\\u0022:\\u0022Transaction-gated Curiosity external result admission\\u0022,\\u0022Body\\u0022:\\u0022The CuriosityEngine slot MAY request GraphRAG or context admission for external model output only after the related brain-slot invocation transaction commits successfully through the subscriber path.\\u0022,\\u0022WorkspaceId\\u0022:\\u0022F:\\\\\\\\GitHub\\\\\\\\McpServer\\u0022,\\u0022Priority\\u0022:\\u0022critical\\u0022,\\u0022Status\\u0022:\\u0022completed\\u0022,\\u0022Notes\\u0022:\\u0022Admission is Curiosity-only and commit-gated.\\u0022,\\u0022AcceptanceCriteria\\u0022:[{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022AC-FR-MCP-130-001\\u0022,\\u0022text\\u0022:\\u0022No model output is returned to the caller until the subscriber commit succeeds.\\u0022,\\u0022isSatisfied\\u0022:true,\\u0022evidence\\u0022:null},{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022AC-FR-MCP-130-002\\u0022,\\u0022text\\u0022:\\u0022If commit fails, times out, or degrades, output is discarded from the response and is not injected into cache or GraphRAG.\\u0022,\\u0022isSatisfied\\u0022:true,\\u0022evidence\\u0022:null},{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022AC-FR-MCP-130-003\\u0022,\\u0022text\\u0022:\\u0022Only CuriosityEngine may request GraphRAG/context admission.\\u0022,\\u0022isSatisfied\\u0022:true,\\u0022evidence\\u0022:null},{\\u0022id\\u0022:\\u0022AC-FR-MCP-130-004\\u0022,\\u0022t