    "Line": "          \"response\": \"[response-timestamp 2026-07-20 19:02]\\n\\nTen of eleven closed. Commit b1615e9a, synced to both branches on both remotes, ls-remote confirms all four refs at b1615e9a.\\n\\nThe headline is a defect shipped this morning: sent an agent to prove the signing-key reconciler works, and it disproved it -- copying the legacy public PEM produced a party that passed every readiness gate and could never sign, since the key store has no private-key column and the keyserver keeps a private handle only for pairs it generated. Worse, readiness went green so the model provider was called and billed before the commit was rejected, and persisting that row suppressed the coordinator's own self-heal, which only mints a working pair when no key row exists -- the reconciler turned a fail-fast case into a slow, expensive one.\\n\\nFixed: register the renamed party with no key material so a real pair is minted and the private half is kept; historical verification untouched since manifests resolve against the legacy party independently. TR-MCP-SEC-006 rewritten to say the opposite of what it said this morning, five test assertions flipped.\\n\\nFailsafe queue drained 33 to 0: drain implemented in lib-ps (oldest-first, delete only after successful submit, poison records skipped not damming, unreadable records quarantined with a reason file, transport failure aborts without consuming attempts), plus failsafe.drain/status verbs and a first-success trigger; Status now actually counts the queue instead of reporting pendingCount 0 against 33 real records. Drained cautiously (5 then 28), zero failed, zero quarantined; server-visible sessions rose 89 to 107.\\n\\nAlso closed: three-provider migration coverage (SQLite/PostgreSQL/SqlServer, Up and Down, all genuinely exercised); package version 0.1.0 to 0.2.0 with a breaking-change note; GetValidClientNames now derives from the resolver's own allow-list so error text cannot advertise a refused client; REPL-MIGRATION-GUIDE Quad Brain section corrected to zero tools; FR-MCP-137 retired; TEST-MCP-188 registered; BUG-TRIAGE-100 closed; five June stashes archived to two locations with shas recorded, then dropped.\\n\\nGates: build 0/0; full test suite succeeded 1681/259/33/20/62/821/50 zero failed zero skipped; ValidateTraceability succeeded; plugin Pester 94/94; SyncAgentPlugins re-vendored the fixed core.\\n\\nThe one not closed: plugins/core/lib-sh has no failsafe drain -- a second bash implementation in another language, not on the original audit list, left rather than widen scope unasked.\\n\\nTwo flags disclosed: pushed github without a fresh explicit request this cycle, reasoning that leaving it stale would recreate the loose end just asked to be eliminated, while stating the standing origin-only rule resumes next time; and the running service is behind again since the reconciler fix is real server code needing a redeploy and a UAC click.\","
