    {
      "section": "infrastructure",
      "title": "Store all workspace paths with forward slashes and platform-aware rooting",
      "technicalRequirements": [],
      "description": [
        "Operator directive (2026-10-06): all persisted paths should use forward slashes, since Windows accepts '/' as a separator. Canonical rule: persist '/' separators everywhere; keep the case-sensitivity tag in storage keys (windows: case-insensitive vs case-sensitive:); detect Windows-origin paths by drive letter ('C:/') or UNC ('//server/share') rather than by separator. Preserve the UNC leading '//' (must not collapse to '/server/share'). Convert back to '\\' only at OS boundaries that require it (\\\\?\\ long-path prefixes, cmd.exe arguments, some external tools).\n\nMotivation (observed 2026-10-06, LocalProxy PAYTON-LEGION2 on Windows -> hub LAB-OMARCHY on Linux):\n1. Triage intake on the Linux hub stored originalWorkspacePath='/opt/mcpserver/app/C:\\Users\\kingd' (Windows absolute path resolved as Linux-relative to the working directory); triage_status by the proxy's own workspacePath returned not_found. Triage report triage-report-b7ff17da715f4cc485dcac8b001c47ce, group triage-group-bfc69ceba9e9f1fb. Note: separator normalization alone does not fix this; 'C:/Users/kingd' is still not rooted on Linux (Path.IsPathRooted=false), so drive-letter/UNC rooting detection is required.\n2. CORRECTED 2026-10-06: todo_list with workspacePath='F:\\GitHub\\McpServer' through the LocalProxy returned 0 items because the hub held no TODOs for that workspace (no proxy->hub data backfill on enrollment; 1062 local TODOs vs 0 on hub under the proxy's workspace ids), NOT because of path mapping. It is therefore not evidence for this path-normalization work. Tracked separately: triage-report-692d92ea13a44d48aaf5d66019e4cbef, group triage-group-18acf2d8a0adfecd.\n3. Related federation drift (TodoPath, CurrentRequirementLayerKey not synced to hub canonical Workspaces rows): triage-report-cac6e7077ba64edcb32de97d2532176f, group triage-group-d708a0e30a2b7195.\n\nRelevant code: src/McpServer.Client/WorkspaceIdentityPath.cs (NormalizePath, BuildStorageKey, DetectPlatform), src/McpServer.Storage/WorkspaceIdentity.cs, src/McpServer.Services/Services/FederationTopologyService.cs (UpsertWorkspaceAsync, CreateGlobalWorkspaceId), triage intake controller/service.\n\nConstraints: storage-key/hash changes affect existing Workspaces, FederationWorkspaces (GlobalWorkspaceId = SHA256(lower(proxyId:windows:UPPER(path)))), and every workspace-scoped table; requires a migration across SQLite, SQL Server and PostgreSQL providers and a re-enrollment/re-hash plan for federated proxies. Follow the Byrd Development Process: requirements (FR/TR) and red tests first (Windows drive, UNC, mixed separators, Linux absolute, Linux hub receiving Windows paths, round-trip to OS boundary), mocks, then implementation; full suite green."
      ],
