            "title": "Canonical TODO and Session Identifier Conventions",
            "updatedAt": "2026-11-10T13:29:13.7877508-06:00",
            "priority": "medium",
            "description": "The server shall enforce canonical identifier conventions for newly created TODO and session log payloads:\n\n- Persisted TODO IDs must match either uppercase kebab-case ending in a three-digit sequence suffix (for example `PHASE0-REMOTE-001` or `MCP-TODO-CREATE-001`) or `ISSUE-{number}` for canonical GitHub-backed TODOs.\n- Create requests may use `ISSUE-NEW` only as a temporary server-side alias for immediate GitHub-backed TODO creation; persisted TODO IDs must still be canonical.\n- Session IDs must match `<Agent>-<yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ>-<suffix>` and be prefixed by the exact `sourceType`/`agent`.\n- Request IDs must match `req-<yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ>-<slugOrOrdinal>`.\n\nValidation failures return client-visible errors without mutating persisted data.\n\n**Covered by:** `TodoValidator`, `TodoService`, `SqliteTodoService`, `TodoCreationService`, `SessionLogIdentifierValidator`, `SessionLogController`, `SessionLogService`",
            "status": "pending",
            "createdAt": "2026-11-10T13:29:13.7877189-06:00",
            "id": "FR-MCP-061"
          }
        },
