            "description": "Normalize durable identifier strings before computing derived hashes. Use pinned-directory-relative Windows NT and POSIX operations for contained creation, open, replacement, rollback deletion, and empty-directory removal. Resolve physical paths through finite cancellable native operations used asynchronously by persistence and federation. Snapshot only regular files with no-follow nonblocking stat enforcement. Scope SQLite open and query work with exact restoration of managed, EF, connection-string, native timeout, and handler state; preserve real provider exceptions. Discover repository roots from stable assembly or source metadata and bound process plus pipe-drain lifetime for full process trees.\n**Covered by:** FR: FR-MCP-USECASE-015; TEST: TEST-MCP-USECASE-018",
            "status": "pending",
