          "original": {
            "updatedAt": "2026-11-10T13:32:30.7098579-06:00",
            "title": "Handle-relative containment, bounded providers, canonical identity, and hermetic evidence",
            "description": "Normalize durable identifier strings before computing derived hashes. Use pinned-directory-relative Windows NT and POSIX operations for contained creation, open, replacement, rollback deletion, and empty-directory removal. Resolve physical paths through finite cancellable native operations used asynchronously by persistence and federation. Snapshot only regular files with no-follow nonblocking stat enforcement. Scope SQLite open and query work with exact restoration of managed, EF, connection-string, native timeout, and handler state; preserve real provider exceptions. Discover repository roots from stable assembly or source metadata and bound process plus pipe-drain lifetime for full process trees.",
            "id": "TR-MCP-USECASE-017",
            "acceptanceCriteria": [
              {
                "text": "McpDbContext normalizes all durable identity fields before computing hashes, and every derived hash matches the exact final persisted value.",
                "id": "TR-MCP-USECASE-017-AC001",
                "isSatisfied": false
              },
              {
                "text": "WorkspaceContainedFileSystem performs Windows creation/open/deletion and Linux contained mutation relative to pinned parents, validates the opened object, and never follows a reparse or symbolic link.",
                "id": "TR-MCP-USECASE-017-AC002",
                "isSatisfied": false
              },
              {
                "text": "SaveChangesAsync and federation upsert await finite cancellation-aware physical-resolution APIs whose native implementations do not use abandoned Task.Run work, accumulating threads, or repeated uncancellable Directory.Exists calls.",
                "id": "TR-MCP-USECASE-017-AC003",
                "isSatisfied": false
              },
              {
                "text": "Linux file open uses no-follow and nonblocking semantics plus descriptor stat/type checks so FIFOs, devices, sockets, and directories cannot block or enter snapshots.",
                "id": "TR-MCP-USECASE-017-AC004",
                "isSatisfied": false
              },
              {
                "text": "SQLite scoped operations preserve and restore exact connection, EF, connection-string, native busy-timeout, and busy-handler state without deriving native state from DefaultTimeout.",
                "id": "TR-MCP-USECASE-017-AC005",
                "isSatisfied": false
              },
              {
                "text": "SQLite opening is performed by a bounded owned worker/lifetime mechanism that covers pre-handle blocking and proves no worker, handle, pooled-state, callback, or interrupt leaks across cancellation and repeated calls.",
                "id": "TR-MCP-USECASE-017-AC006",
                "isSatisfied": false
              },
              {
                "text": "Cancellation classification is based on provider cancellation evidence and exception type/state rather than token state alone for SQLite, SQL Server, and PostgreSQL.",
                "id": "TR-MCP-USECASE-017-AC007",
                "isSatisfied": false
              },
              {
                "text": "Evidence tests resolve a validated root from assembly/source anchors without MCP_REPOSITORY_ROOT and process execution bounds parent exit, both stream drains, and the descendant process tree.",
                "id": "TR-MCP-USECASE-017-AC008",
                "isSatisfied": false
              },
              {
                "text": "Evidence inventories are regenerated only after finalization and verified by an independent parsing pass with exact command-to-output and TRX outcome accounting.",
                "id": "TR-MCP-USECASE-017-AC009",
                "isSatisfied": false
              },
              {
                "text": "Historical migration bytes and previously approved trust, preflight, cleanup, non-Windows, trailer, and line-ending guarantees remain unchanged.",
                "id": "TR-MCP-USECASE-017-AC010",
                "isSatisfied": false
              }
            ],
